ase or conversion speed matters;\n  tokenised vaulting only (mandatory under PCI-DSS).\n  - Tokenised vaulting — store the PSP token, never the card, for one-click reuse. The floor of this capability; mandatory when `compliance` includes PCI-DSS.", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 60, "end": 68, "text": "  - Level 1 — full / partial refunds: reverse a charge in whole or part via the PSP. The floor.\n  - Level 2 — chargeback handling: receive and process issuer-initiated reversals. Add when `shape.monetization: monetized`.\n  - Level 3 — dispute-evidence workflow: assemble and submit evidence with an audit trail. Add when `nfr.observability >= high`, or `compliance` includes PCI-DSS.\n- **Saved Methods / One-Click** — when repeat purchase or conversion speed matters;\n  tokenised vaulting only (mandatory under PCI-DSS).\n  - Tokenised vaulting — store the PSP token, never the card, for one-click reuse. The floor of this capability; mandatory when `compliance` includes PCI-DSS.\n  - One-click checkout — charge a saved token without re-entry. Add when `shape.monetization: monetized` and repeat purchase matters.\n\n## Where it goes wrong (proposed)"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261018-004", "issue": 613, "play": "/vision", "question": "Are Apple Pay and Google Pay part of launch?", "answer": "Yes. The shop has a mobile app, so wallets are in.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper (/vision)", "decided_at": "2026-10-18T19:01:24Z", "trace": [{"asked": "Who are the shop's users, and where do they use it?", "found": "The public, on web and mobile.", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/profile.yaml", "start": 6, "end": 8, "fingerprint": "sha256:ea4be5fa81c618857bc9e02deec8eb38b782ca54725daf5ca6c452edfeaf77fd", "text": "    users: public\n    monetization: paywall\n    surfaces: [web, mobile]", "version": null, "around": {"start": 3, "end": 11, "text": "  state: set\n  shape:\n    stage: public\n    users: public\n    monet