, "end": 11, "text": "  state: set\n  shape:\n    stage: public\n    users: public\n    monetization: paywall\n    surfaces: [web, mobile]\n  nfr:\n    performance:   { level: high, gate: \"p95 page load under 2 s\" }\n    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }"}}}, {"asked": "Which domain covers sign-in, and what decides its parts?", "found": "User management. Its parts are picked by the profile: the users, the surfaces, security, accessibility and compliance.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/user-management.md", "start": 4, "end": 6, "fingerprint": "sha256:e295931e169cff7ce46dfc8847509d1797cde5adcfe9ec5770941dfd04f3273e", "text": "conditions:\n  trigger: \"the product needs accounts, login, profiles, roles, or access control\"\n  selection_keys: [shape.users, shape.surfaces, nfr.security, nfr.accessibility, compliance]", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 1, "end": 9, "text": "---\nid: domains/user-management\ntitle: \"User Management: capabilities and when to include each (profile-driven)\"\nconditions:\n  trigger: \"the product needs accounts, login, profiles, roles, or access control\"\n  selection_keys: [shape.users, shape.surfaces, nfr.security, nfr.accessibility, compliance]\nprovenance: seeded\n---\n"}}}, {"asked": "What security level and compliance does the profile set?", "found": "Security is high; PCI-DSS and GDPR are in force.", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/profile.yaml", "start": 11, "end": 14, "fingerprint": "sha256:792104d6b9ddcfb5eb567bd3e3e3173bce8d6c5a3d5296a223484131bb3c935a", "text": "    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }\n    accessibility: { level: high, gate: \"WCAG 2.1 AA\" }\n    privacy:       { level: high, gate: \"PII encrypted at rest and in transit\" }\n  compliance: [PCI-DSS, GDPR]", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 14, "text": "    surfaces: [web, mobile]\n  nfr:\n    performance:   { level: high, gate: \"p95 page load under 2 s\" }\n    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }\n    accessibility: { level: high, gate: \"WCAG 2.1 AA\" }\n    privacy:       { level: high, gate: \"PII encrypted at rest and in transit\" }\n  compliance: [PCI-DSS, GDPR]"}}}, {"asked": "Which sign-in methods do those values select?", "found": "Email and password is the floor; social login because the users are public; MFA because security is high and PCI-DSS is in force.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/user-management.md", "start": 44, "end": 47, "fingerprint": "sha256:001365eca3509fec072c26b605372ed8719be8d71efd80c08e780fb6aee613b9", "text": "- **Authentication** — include when users sign in.\n  - Email & password — the default credential login (the floor).\n  - Social login — when `shape.users: public` and signup friction matters.\n  - MFA — when `nfr.security >= high`, or `compliance` includes SOC2 / HIPAA / PCI-DSS.", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 41, "end": 50, "text": "Read each line as \"include X when {profile condition}\". Start at the floor; add\nonly when a profile dimension calls for it.\n\n- **Authentication** — include when users sign in.\n  - Email & password — the default credential login (the floor).\n  - Social login — when `shape.users: public` and signup friction matters.\n  - MFA — when `nfr.security >= high`, or `compliance` includes SOC2 / HIPAA / PCI-DSS.\n  - Passwordless — when `nfr.security >= high` and you want to remove password risk entirely.\n  - Enterprise SSO — when the user base is organizations (B2B), or `compliance` requires federated identity.\n- **Registration** — include when users create accounts."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261018-009", "issue": 613, "play": "/understand", "question": "Does the shop need MFA at launch?", "answer": "Yes. Security is high and PCI-DSS is in force; either one brings MFA.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper (/understand)