+Story #659 under Feature #653 (feature plan item 6): every decision an agent makes names the memory it came from — tier, file, lines and fingerprint — in one shape built on the existing resolution trace format; agents write it to the issue's short-term memory; a script checks each named source exists and its fingerprint still matches; the drive review record carries the sources. First, three notes from the PR #675 review: the review tool's mockup gains the Memory and ADRs section (the memory page is part of the committed design); contract version 3 states that a waiting draft is hidden from lookups; the design says the Memory and ADRs section (#664) needs Garura-side work too. Decided in ADR 035 §6.
