+    "waiting_drafts_are_hidden": "A lookup (find, search, read) never returns a memory update that waits for a person: updates are kept apart in the issue's short-term memory, and only an applied update's written file can be found. Otherwise a draft from the web or the model would drive the work with no person in between (ADR 036). Decision records are not memory either: a lookup never returns them, so an agent never decides from its own earlier decision.",
+    "cite_reads_its_sources": "cite records nothing unless every step's source exists in its tier and the text of its lines still has its fingerprint.",
+    "citations_problems": "Without check, problems is empty. With check, each record with no trace is no_source (step and source null); each step whose source file or lines are gone is source_missing; each step whose source text no longer matches its fingerprint is source_changed. A problem's step is the step's number in the trace, from 1. Every record and problem is of the request's issue. A problem's now is the text those lines hold now, and now_around the lines around them now; both are null when the lines are gone.",
